From 4cdf41a0809ab6db70a7108b788427ecb5806ff7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kevin <neonc0in@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 20:12:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Wayland: only accept the output mode flagged current

wl_output.mode may be sent once per supported mode, not just for the active
one -- cosmic-comp sends 29 for a typical monitor, current flagged second and
640x480 last. The handler ignored the flags argument, so the last mode always
won and every screen query returned 640x480 regardless of the real resolution.

Filter on WL_OUTPUT_MODE_CURRENT. Verified: screens now report 3440x1440 and
2560x1440 instead of 640x480.

Unrelated to layer shell; affects any compositor that advertises full mode
lists, and is worth sending upstream on its own.
---
 platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
index 752adfd573..1ec3839069 100644
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
@@ -1374,6 +1374,15 @@ void WaylandThread::_wl_output_on_mode(void *data, struct wl_output *wl_output,
 	ScreenState *ss = (ScreenState *)data;
 	ERR_FAIL_NULL(ss);
 
+	// A compositor may advertise every mode the output supports, not just the
+	// active one -- cosmic-comp sends all 29 for a typical monitor. Only the mode
+	// flagged current describes the screen we are actually on; without this check
+	// the last mode in the list wins, which is usually the smallest the display
+	// can do (640x480), and every screen query is wrong from then on.
+	if (!(flags & WL_OUTPUT_MODE_CURRENT)) {
+		return;
+	}
+
 	ss->pending_data.size.width = width;
 	ss->pending_data.size.height = height;
 
